        "purpose": "transcribing",
        "value": "兵卒百三拾六人"
      },
      {
        "purpose": "modern_jp_reading",
        "value": "兵卒　百三十六人（へいそつ　ひゃくさんじゅうろくにん）"
      },
      {
        "purpose": "english_translation",
        "value": "Rank-and-file troops (heisotsu): 136 men. The figure prints in the lower register of the same column as the 133 soldiers above it, because the next domain's ○鞠山藩 marker already fills the column to the left and left the compositor no room for a second value column. The closing 人 inked only weakly — its stroke-head at the top and the tail of the right-falling stroke survive — but it is the counter 人, not punctuation. Together with the soldiers above, Matsukawa's return comes to 269 men."
      },
      {
        "purpose": "identifying",
        "value": "松川兵卒"
